## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of reproducibility, determinism, and data lineage in a beginner-friendly setting. Emphasizes auditability and simple tests.

## Key Concepts
- Deterministic feature engineering
- Data lineage and reproducibility IDs
- Minimal, auditable API design
- Lightweight explainability vectors

## Code Example
```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');
function computeReproScore(userId, region, modelVersion, seed) {
  const input = `${userId}|${region}|${modelVersion}|${seed}`;
  const hash = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(input).digest('hex');
  const n = parseInt(hash.slice(0, 8), 16);
  return (n % 1000) / 10; // deterministic score 0-99.9
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test drift in reproducibility across model_version updates?
- How would you secure seeds and input digests to protect privacy while enabling audits?

